Yes. And after checking the current Porkbun + Cloudflare capabilities, I would make the TinyTools domain system **more selective than “every tool gets a `.xyz`.”**

## The domain lifecycle I would use

```text
IDEA
  ↓
BUILD + TEST
  ↓
FREE INCUBATION
tool-name.<your-account>.workers.dev
  ↓
passes basic quality gates
  ↓
TINYTOOLS PRODUCTION
tool-name.tinytools.xyz
  ↓
shows meaningful usage/search/agent traffic
  ↓
STANDALONE PRODUCT
goodname.xyz
  ↓
becomes genuinely valuable
  ↓
PREMIUM IDENTITY
goodname.com
```

That gives Hydra something extremely useful: **domain acquisition becomes a promotion event rather than part of initial deployment.**

### Why this is better

A domain is not actually required to test whether an API is useful. Every Cloudflare Worker automatically gets a free `*.workers.dev` endpoint. ([Cloudflare Docs][1])

And once you own one TinyTools root domain, you can have:

```text
pdfmerge.tinytools.xyz
domaincheck.tinytools.xyz
htmlclean.tinytools.xyz
timestamp.tinytools.xyz
jsonrepair.tinytools.xyz
currency.tinytools.xyz
...
```

for effectively **zero additional domain-registration cost**.

Then only products that show evidence of life get:

```text
jsonrepair.xyz
```

and perhaps eventually:

```text
jsonrepair.com
```

This is much more sensible for a factory capable of creating thousands of utilities.

