# The clever bit: Cloudflare should be created BEFORE changing Porkbun

When you buy:

```text
repairjson.xyz
```

Hydra does:

### 1. Register through Porkbun

Porkbun becomes the registrar.

### 2. Add domain to Cloudflare

Cloudflare has:

```http
POST /zones
```

which creates the zone and returns its assigned Cloudflare nameservers. ([Cloudflare Docs][6])

For example:

```text
ada.ns.cloudflare.com
bob.ns.cloudflare.com
```

### 3. Tell Porkbun to use those nameservers

Porkbun's current API can read and **replace nameservers at the registry level**. ([porkbun.com][4])

So Hydra sends the two nameservers back to Porkbun.

```text
Porkbun registrar

repairjson.xyz
     NS → ada.ns.cloudflare.com
     NS → bob.ns.cloudflare.com
```

Porkbun is now essentially just holding ownership/renewal.

Everything else becomes Cloudflare.

Cloudflare says a zone initially remains `pending` until the registrar points the domain at the assigned Cloudflare nameservers. ([Cloudflare Docs][6])

