# Then Cloudflare takes over

Once active:

```text
Cloudflare
├── DNS
├── TLS certificates
├── Worker
├── cache
├── WAF
├── redirects
├── analytics
├── D1
├── R2
├── KV
├── Durable Objects
└── whatever else tool needs
```

If the application itself is a Worker, **Cloudflare Custom Domains are particularly nice**.

When Hydra attaches:

```text
repairjson.xyz
```

to the Worker, Cloudflare can automatically create the DNS records and issue the required TLS certificate. ([Cloudflare Docs][7])

Thus no:

```text
generate cert
upload cert
configure nginx
create A records
configure load balancer
```

It's effectively:

```text
Worker
   +
Cloudflare zone
   +
Custom Domain
   =
live HTTPS product
```

